diff --git a/kalman/index.html b/kalman/index.html
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..55a466d3fe2d63eb30cff476c98ed664a725c7f3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/kalman/index.html
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+<!doctype html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
+  <meta name="description" content="Take an underwater robot through a seeded mission and discover how a Kalman filter turns noisy depth fixes into navigation.">
+  <title>ABYSS — A Kalman navigation lab</title>
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
+  <script defer src="model.js"></script><script defer src="app.js"></script>
+</head>
+<body>
+<a class="skip" href="#controls">Skip to mission controls</a>
+<header class="masthead"><a class="brand" href="../secret/" aria-label="Back to Secret projects"><span class="brand-mark">◈</span> ABYSS <span class="brand-sub">/ NAVIGATION LAB</span></a><a class="back" href="../secret/">← Secret projects</a></header>
+<main>
+  <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="title"><div><p class="eyebrow">ROBOSUB-INSPIRED / EXPERIMENT 04</p><h1 id="title">Find your way.<br><em>Through uncertainty.</em></h1><p class="lede">A robot. An imperfect sensor. One better estimate.<br>Take the controls and discover how a Kalman filter navigates the unknown.</p></div><div class="mission-stamp"><span class="stamp-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌖</span><span>MISSION 001<br><strong>THE DEEP TRANSECT</strong><br>60 seconds · depth navigation</span></div></section>
+  <noscript><div class="fallback">This interactive lab needs JavaScript. A Kalman filter predicts depth and vertical velocity from known acceleration, then corrects that prediction using noisy depth fixes. The teal uncertainty band represents its assumed 95% interval, not a guarantee. The model and references below explain the method.</div></noscript>
+  <div class="workspace">
+    <section class="mission panel" aria-labelledby="scene-title">
+      <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="scene-title"><span class="dot"></span> LIVE MISSION</h2><span id="mission-state" class="badge">READY / PAUSED</span></div>
+      <div class="scene-wrap"><canvas id="scene" role="img" aria-label="Depth versus mission time: truth is a white dashed line with square markers, fixes are amber circles, estimate is a teal solid line with diamond marker, and the shaded ribbon is its assumed 95 percent depth interval." aria-describedby="scene-caption live-text"></canvas><div class="scene-heading" aria-hidden="true"><span>ABYSS / AUV–01</span><strong>DEPTH TRANSECT</strong></div><div class="scene-note" aria-hidden="true">PROCESSED POSITION FIXES<br>NOT GPS OR RAW SONAR</div></div>
+      <div class="legend"><span class="truth-key">┄□ Truth</span><span class="sensor-key">○ Measurement</span><span class="filter-key">━◇ Estimate</span><span class="dead-key">┄ Dead reckoning</span><span class="band-key">▰ Assumed 95% interval</span></div>
+      <p class="caption" id="scene-caption">Side-view depth plot, positive downward. Horizontal position represents mission time, not physical travel. Gate, slalom, and bin are illustrative mission milestones.</p>
+      <div class="transport" id="controls" tabindex="-1"><button id="play" class="primary" disabled>▶ Start mission</button><button id="step" disabled>Step +0.2 s</button><button id="reset" disabled>↺ Reset</button><label class="speed-label" for="speed">Playback<select id="speed"><option value="1">1×</option><option value="4">4×</option><option value="10">10×</option></select></label></div>
+      <div class="progress-row"><span id="clock">00.0 / 60.0 s</span><progress id="progress" max="300" value="0" aria-label="Mission progress"></progress><span id="stage">01 / GATE APPROACH</span></div>
+      <p id="event" class="event">Ready to descend. Start the mission, or step through one correction.</p>
+    </section>
+    <aside class="setup panel" aria-labelledby="setup-title"><div class="panel-head"><h2 id="setup-title">MISSION SETUP</h2><span class="micro">REPEATABLE BY DESIGN</span></div>
+      <label class="field-label" for="scenario">01 / Choose conditions</label><select id="scenario"><option value="nominal">Nominal · noisy fixes</option><option value="dropout">Dropout · no fixes, 20–36 s</option><option value="current">Current · disturbance, 20–40 s</option><option value="bias">Sensor bias · +2 m after 20 s</option></select>
+      <p id="scenario-help" class="help">Random disturbances, unbiased fixes. The default Q and R match the actual noise.</p>
+      <fieldset><legend>02 / The real world</legend><label for="sensor-noise">Actual sensor σ <output id="sensor-value"></output></label><input id="sensor-noise" type="range" min="0.1" max="4" step="0.1" value="0.8"><label for="accel-noise">Actual acceleration σ <output id="accel-value"></output></label><input id="accel-noise" type="range" min="0" max="0.2" step="0.01" value="0.08"><p class="help">Standard deviations. These change the physical mission and its measurements.</p></fieldset>
+      <fieldset><legend>03 / What the filter believes</legend><label for="r-noise">Measurement variance R <output id="r-value"></output></label><input id="r-noise" type="range" min="-2" max="1.20412" step="0.01" value="-0.19382"><label for="q-noise">Acceleration variance q → Q <output id="q-value"></output></label><input id="q-noise" type="range" min="-4" max="-0.79588" step="0.01" value="-2.19382"><p class="help">Higher R trusts fixes less. Higher q allows more motion uncertainty. Tuning replays the <strong>same sensor data</strong>.</p></fieldset>
+      <div class="seed-row"><label for="seed">04 / Random seed<input id="seed" type="number" value="42" min="0" max="4294967295" step="1" inputmode="numeric"></label><button id="replay">Replay seed</button></div><p class="help">Any setting change pauses and rewinds. Same seed + real-world settings = same data.</p>
+      <button id="pin" class="wide">＋ Save tuning as baseline</button><button id="clear-baseline" class="subtle wide" hidden>Clear baseline</button><p id="baseline-note" class="help">Save a baseline, change R or q, then run again to compare.</p>
+    </aside>
+  </div>
+  <section class="telemetry" aria-label="Live telemetry"><div><span>TRUE DEPTH</span><strong id="true-depth">7.00 <small>m</small></strong></div><div><span>MEASURED DEPTH</span><strong id="measured-depth">— <small>m</small></strong></div><div class="teal"><span>ESTIMATED DEPTH</span><strong id="estimated-depth">7.00 <small>m</small></strong></div><div><span>VERTICAL VELOCITY</span><strong id="velocity">0.10 <small>m/s</small></strong></div><div><span>95% HALF-WIDTH</span><strong id="confidence">1.96 <small>m</small></strong></div><div><span>ACTUAL DEPTH ERROR</span><strong id="actual-error">0.00 <small>m</small></strong></div></section>
+  <p id="live-text" class="semantic-readout">At 0 seconds: true depth 7 m; estimate 7 m; no fix yet; assumed 95% depth interval ±1.96 m. Mission paused.</p>
+  <p id="announcement" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
+  <div class="analysis-grid">
+    <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="error-title"><div class="panel-head"><h2 id="error-title">CONFIDENCE ≠ ACCURACY</h2><span class="micro">DEPTH ERROR / METERS</span></div><canvas id="error-chart" role="img" aria-label="Signed estimate error against assumed plus and minus 1.96 sigma bounds; baseline error is dashed purple if saved." aria-describedby="error-text"></canvas><p id="error-text" class="caption">The white line is actual estimate minus truth. Teal bounds express confidence under the assumed model. Bias or current can push error outside them.</p></section>
+    <section class="panel score-panel" aria-labelledby="score-title"><div class="panel-head"><h2 id="score-title">NAVIGATION SCORECARD</h2><span class="micro" id="score-time">ELAPSED DATA</span></div><table><caption class="sr-only">Root mean squared depth error for the elapsed mission</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Method</th><th scope="col">RMSE <small>(m)</small></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><span class="sensor-key">○</span> Raw fixes</th><td id="rmse-sensor">—</td></tr><tr class="filter-row"><th scope="row"><span class="filter-key">◇</span> Kalman estimate</th><td id="rmse-filter">—</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span class="dead-key">┄</span> Dead reckoning</th><td id="rmse-dead">—</td></tr><tr id="baseline-row" hidden><th scope="row">Saved baseline</th><td id="rmse-baseline">—</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="help">RMSE = typical depth error. Fixes score only when available; estimate and dead reckoning score every step. Lower is better; improvement is not guaranteed.</p><p id="coverage" class="coverage">Interval coverage: —</p></section>
+  </div>
+  <section id="summary" class="summary panel" hidden aria-labelledby="summary-title"><p class="eyebrow">TRANSECT COMPLETE / 60 SECONDS</p><h2 id="summary-title">Mission debrief</h2><p id="summary-text"></p><p id="summary-compare"></p><button id="again">↺ Replay this mission</button></section>
+  <section class="learning" aria-labelledby="learn-title"><div class="learning-intro"><p class="eyebrow">INSIDE THE ESTIMATOR</p><h2 id="learn-title">Predict. Listen.<br><em>Correct.</em></h2><p>The filter never sees the white truth trace. It combines a motion model with imperfect depth fixes, and tracks how uncertain that estimate is.</p><p class="lesson-prompt"><strong>Try this:</strong> Run dropout to 20 s. Step forward and watch the interval widen. Then save a baseline and increase R: why does the filter hesitate when fixes return?</p></div><div class="lesson-cards"><article><span class="lesson-number">01</span><div><h3>Predict the next state</h3><p>Depth advances using vertical velocity and known acceleration. Uncertain acceleration adds covariance Q.</p><code>d⁻ = d + h·v + ½h²·u<br>v⁻ = v + h·u<br>P⁻ = FPFᵀ + Q</code></div></article><article><span class="lesson-number">02</span><div><h3>Weigh the new fix</h3><p>The innovation is the fix minus predicted depth. Gain K balances predicted uncertainty against assumed sensor variance R.</p><code>y = z − d⁻ &nbsp; S = P⁻₀₀ + R<br>K = [P⁻₀₀, P⁻₁₀]ᵀ / S</code></div></article><article><span class="lesson-number">03</span><div><h3>Correct, without seeing truth</h3><p>Move depth and velocity by K·y. A missing fix skips correction; the prediction and its growing uncertainty remain.</p><code>x = x⁻ + K·y<br>P = (I−KH)P⁻(I−KH)ᵀ + KRKᵀ</code></div></article></div></section>
+  <section class="worked panel" aria-labelledby="worked-title"><div class="panel-head"><h2 id="worked-title">ONE CORRECTION, UNPACKED</h2><span id="worked-time" class="micro">STEP TO SEE LIVE NUMBERS</span></div><div id="worked-numbers" class="worked-grid"><div><span>PREDICTION</span><strong>What motion suggests</strong></div><div><span>INNOVATION</span><strong>Fix − prediction</strong></div><div><span>POSITION GAIN</span><strong>How much to trust the fix</strong></div><div><span>CORRECTION</span><strong>Prediction + gain × innovation</strong></div></div><details><summary>See a simple exact example</summary><p>Let h = 1 s, acceleration u = 0, Q = 0, R = 1 m², initial [depth, velocity] = [0, 0], and P = identity. Predicting gives P⁻ = [[2, 1], [1, 1]]. A fix z = 3 m gives gain [2/3, 1/3]. The corrected state is [2 m, 1 m/s] and P = [[2/3, 1/3], [1/3, 2/3]]. Depth moves two thirds of the way toward the fix.</p></details></section>
+  <details class="model-details panel" open><summary>Model, units & honest limits</summary><div class="model-copy"><p><strong>One axis, fixed steps.</strong> State x = [depth (m), vertical velocity (m/s)]. h = 0.2 s; F = [[1,h],[0,1]], B = [h²/2,h]ᵀ, H = [1,0]. Initial state [7,0.1], initial P = diag(1 m², 0.04 m²/s²). Known commanded acceleration is 0.07 cos(0.2t) − 0.035 sin(0.4t) m/s².</p><p><strong>Disturbance-consistent Q.</strong> Actual acceleration disturbance is independent Gaussian noise held constant per step. q is its assumed variance in (m/s²)², and Q = qBBᵀ = q[[h⁴/4,h³/2],[h³/2,h²]]. R is depth-fix variance in m². Standard deviation σ has the original units; variance is σ². The default values are rounded to four significant figures.</p><p><strong>What is a fix?</strong> A simulated, already processed localization depth fix, sampled every 0.2 s. This is not raw sonar range/bearing, underwater GPS, or DVL. No velocity sensor is modeled. Truth is used only for drawing and evaluation. Dead reckoning integrates commands with the same initial state and no fixes.</p><p><strong>Confidence has assumptions.</strong> The ribbon is the marginal depth interval d̂ ± 1.96√P₀₀, approximately 95% for a calibrated Gaussian model. It is not a 2D ellipse or a safety guarantee. Current adds an unknown acceleration of +0.045 m/s² from 20–40 s; bias adds +2 m to fixes after 20 s. Both deliberately violate the zero-mean assumptions. Dropout removes fixes from 20–36 s.</p><p><strong>Learning simulation.</strong> A prescribed depth transect, not closed-loop vehicle control, collision detection, or official RoboSub scoring. The gate, slalom, and bin references are simplified inspiration. Drag, attitude, full vehicle dynamics and correlated sensor errors are outside this model.</p><p class="sources">Further reading: <a href="https://www.cs.unc.edu/~welch/media/pdf/kalman_intro.pdf">Welch & McGee · Kalman introduction</a> · <a href="https://www.bzarg.com/p/how-a-kalman-filter-works-in-pictures/">Kalman filters in pictures</a> · <a href="https://robonation.gitbook.io/robosub-resources/section-3-autonomy-challenge/3.2-task-descriptions">RoboSub task inspiration</a> · <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/">WCAG 2.2</a></p></div></details>
+</main><footer class="footer"><a href="../secret/">← Back to Secret projects</a><span>ABYSS / BUILT TO MAKE UNCERTAINTY VISIBLE</span><span>RoboSub-inspired. Independently made.</span></footer>
