@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+# ABYSS / Kalman navigation lab
+
+A complete static activity at `kalman/`, launched through Secret's fourth project card. No build, CDN, dependencies, service credentials, or backend are required. Changes are contained in this working copy and are uncommitted and unpublished.
+
+## Preview
+
+From this working copy:
+
+```powershell
+node kalman/preview.cjs
+```
+
+Open [the lab](http://127.0.0.1:8312/kalman/) or [Secret](http://127.0.0.1:8312/secret/). The preview server binds only to local loopback. An alternative static server can serve the repository root. The activity can also load from its HTML file with local relative assets. The preview server is for static pages; use the existing private-upload preview server for upload API testing.
+
+## Using the activity
+
+1. Start the paused 60-second mission, or step through one 0.2-second prediction/correction. Pause, reset, and 1×/4×/10× playback are available. All controls use native keyboard behavior; no document-wide keyboard shortcuts are installed.
+2. Distinguish white dashed truth/squares, amber measurement circles, teal estimate/diamond and interval ribbon, and purple dashed dead reckoning. Read equivalent numerical text below the telemetry. The scene's horizontal axis is time, not physical distance.
+3. Select dropout, current, or sensor bias to challenge the model. Dropout removes fixes from 20–36 seconds. Current adds unknown acceleration from 20–40 seconds. Bias offsets fixes by +2 meters after 20 seconds.
+4. Change actual sensor/acceleration standard deviations to change the generated mission. Change assumed R/q to change only the estimator. Any setting change pauses and rewinds.
+5. Save a tuning baseline, change R or q, and replay. A labeled purple baseline trace, scorecard row, and completed-mission comparison use identical measurements and identical elapsed-time scoring. Real-world changes clear the baseline because the data changed.
+6. Read the live worked correction, exact introductory example, learner prompt, error-versus-confidence chart, and endpoint debrief.
+
+## Numerical implementation
+
+`model.js` is shared unchanged between the browser and Node tests. The state is depth/vertical velocity with known commanded acceleration. Each independent Gaussian acceleration disturbance is held constant over one fixed step; Q = qBBᵀ matches that model. Fixes measure depth with H = [1,0]. Joseph covariance correction maintains numerical stability. Truth is used for drawing and evaluation, never to correct the filter. Dead reckoning uses the same initial state and commands, without fixes.
+
+The confidence ribbon is the marginal depth interval estimate ±1.96√P₀₀, under the assumed Gaussian model. Actual error and empirical coverage are reported separately. Fix RMSE excludes missing fixes; estimator and dead-reckoning RMSE include every simulated step. No improvement guarantee is claimed.
+
+Seed 42, default actual noise and tuning, 300 steps:
+
+| Scenario | Fix RMSE (m) | Filter RMSE (m) | Dead reckoning RMSE (m) | Interval coverage | Fixes |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| Nominal | 0.829370 | 0.192692 | 4.906346 | 99.7% | 300 |
+| Dropout | 0.840181 | 0.236344 | 4.906346 | 98.3% | 220 |
+| Current | 0.829370 | 0.351296 | 15.916042 | 76.0% | 300 |
+| Bias | 1.795452 | 1.617936 | 4.906346 | 33.3% | 300 |
+
+These are calculated outputs for this synthetic seed, not benchmarks or results from real robots. Numerical assertions lock the fixed values and also test cases without data or fixes.
+
+## Actual verification
+
+Commands executed from this working copy:
+
+```powershell
+node --test tests/*.test.cjs
+node --check kalman/app.js
+node --check kalman/model.js
+node --check kalman/preview.cjs
+node --check tests/kalman.test.cjs
+node --check tests/secret-projects.test.cjs
+git diff --check
+```
+
+The test suite passes **30/30**: 10 numerical tests and 20 existing private-upload/navigation regressions. It verifies the exact h=1, u=0, Q=0, R=1, x=[0,0], P=I, z=3 fixture; x=[2,1], K=[2/3,1/3], P=[[2/3,1/3],[1/3,2/3]]. It also verifies prediction-only dropout, deterministic replay, tuning-independent sensor streams, truth isolation, actual-noise separation, scenario timing, explicit RMSE values, missing-data denominators, and covariance symmetry/PSD/finite values over 100,000 steps. Regression tests include the fourth Secret card/footer and Worker asset routes. Syntax and whitespace checks pass. Git prints only the repository's LF/CRLF conversion notices.
+
+Browser verification used the connected in-app Chromium browser, including real native controls:
+
+- 1440×900, 390×844, and 320×740 were inspected. No page or main-content horizontal overflow; document width is viewport minus the browser's 15-pixel scrollbar. All visible buttons, inputs, and selects have at least 44-pixel height. Sources and navigation links have 44-pixel targets. Canvas data has semantic labels and numerical text equivalents.
+- Secret's card activated with Enter opens `/kalman/` in a new tab, paused at 0.0 seconds. Four cards and matching footer remain visible. The existing homepage/voltage, keyboard, uploads, and Worker journeys pass regression tests.
+- Native Enter activates step, play, pause, reset, and baseline controls. Arrow keys change actual sensor noise and assumed q; End changes R. Focus uses a visible amber outline. Changing actual noise clears baseline and rewinds; changing tuning retains it.
+- All four scenarios reach 60.0 seconds with endpoint summary, disabled play/step, and working replay/reset. For dropout, the UI at 20.0 seconds shows an unavailable fix and prediction only. Stepping to 24.0 seconds grows the half-width from 0.48 to 1.05 meters.
+- Same-data comparison: the first fix remains 6.80 meters as position gain changes from 0.610 to 0.059 at increased R. Completed nominal RMSE changes from a saved baseline of 0.193 to 0.232 meters at R≈16.1. Saving/clearing baseline after the endpoint refreshes the debrief.
+- Reset clears the live correction and restores the ready badge. Resizing and repeated playback keep canvas dimensions bounded. The third cycle corrected intrinsic canvas height feeding into flex layout; the final absolutely positioned canvas cannot enlarge its own container.
+- No browser warnings or JavaScript errors were observed in the final checks. The console renders only on simulation steps or resize and pauses when the document becomes hidden. No performance benchmark was performed.
+
+Artifacts in [work/kalman-verification](work/kalman-verification/): `tests.txt`, `audit-1440.json`, `audit-390.json`, `audit-320.json`, `desktop-ready.jpg`, `desktop-complete.jpg`, `desktop-dropout.jpg`, `desktop-bias.jpg`, `phone-390.jpg`, and `phone-320.jpg`. The viewport screenshots and audits are the primary layout evidence.
+
+## Design rationale
+
+The deep-water palette, refracted light beams, particles, seafloor silhouettes, illustrated thruster-frame vehicle, technical console typography and contrasting serif headline establish the cinematic mission-control direction. These are custom Canvas/CSS elements, without external bitmap assets. Controls remain above the scene and available before motion begins. Truth/fix/estimate shapes, a dedicated error plot, and explicit physical-versus-assumed settings keep the spectacle connected to the learning task. On phones the interface becomes one reading column, with two-row playback controls.
+
+The three-role review ran three cycles: first numerical/functional build (8/10), second revision and broad browser review (provisional 9/10, invalidated by a later canvas-sizing failure), and final layout/state repair with repeated checks (9/10). No rivals, rival reports, shared run infrastructure, publication, or commits were used. Design choices are hypotheses; no user study was performed.
+
+## Limits and unsupported checks
+
+This is one-axis processed localization, not underwater GPS, raw sonar, DVL, full vehicle dynamics, closed-loop control, collision detection, or official RoboSub scoring. The current and bias presets deliberately violate zero-mean model assumptions. Gate/slalom/bin elements are illustrative inspiration.
+
+Browser media-preference emulation and JavaScript disabling are not exposed by this browser surface. Reduced-motion behavior was inspected in source: no passive animation or autoplay, CSS animation/transition disabled by the media query, motion starts only on an explicit play action, and step is available. The semantic `noscript` explanation and static teaching/reference content were inspected in HTML. Neither is claimed as a browser-emulation pass. A real screen reader and a formal WCAG conformance audit were not run. Announcements occur on user actions and endpoint only, not each simulation step.
+
+The static preview does not test deployed Cloudflare services; private-upload regression tests use the existing local test fixtures. Third-party references are not required to load or operate the lab. The Welch/Bishop PDF direct fetch returned 404 through the research tool, while the same canonical URL was available in indexed source results; external availability may vary.
+
+## Files
+
+- New: `kalman/index.html`, `kalman/styles.css`, `kalman/app.js`, `kalman/model.js`, `kalman/preview.cjs`, `tests/kalman.test.cjs`, `DELIVERY.md`, and local verification artifacts.
+- Updated: `secret/index.html`, `tests/secret-projects.test.cjs`, `README.md`, `work/goal-loop-state.md`.
+
+References: [Welch & Bishop](https://www.cs.unc.edu/~welch/media/pdf/kalman_intro.pdf), [Kalman filters in pictures](https://www.bzarg.com/p/how-a-kalman-filter-works-in-pictures/), [RoboSub task inspiration](https://robonation.gitbook.io/robosub-resources/section-3-autonomy-challenge/3.2-task-descriptions), [RoboSub 2026](https://robosub.org/programs/2026/), [WCAG 2.2](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/).
